-- title:
--   Predictions and detector sets of a finite frontier
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a proof that every reflexive real Banach space has the fixed point property for nonexpansive maps: every $F:C\to C$ with $\|Fa-Fb\|\le\|a-b\|$ on a nonempty closed bounded convex set $C$ has a fixed point. The proof assumes a fixed-point-free map, reduces to a minimal invariant set $K$ of diameter $1$, builds an adaptive weighted tree of nonexpansive maps generated by resolvents, and contradicts the minimality through detecting functionals. An ordered tree has finite levels $0,1,2,\dots$ with a single root, and monotone surjective parent maps from level $k+1$ to level $k$; edge weights are positive and sum to $1$ over the children of each parent. Each node carries a nonexpansive selfmap of $K$, and the tree is evaluated bottom-up: a node's value is its map applied to the weighted average of its children's values. Fix a finite frontier with maps $f_p$ and evaluation $\mathrm{ev}$, earlier candidates with parents and points $y_i$, base points $b_j\in K$, and an ultrafilter $\mathcal U$.
--
--   1. **Residual input and prediction.** $r_p(\theta)=b+\sum_i\theta^p_i(y_i-b)$, and
--   $$
--   \mathrm{pred}_b(\theta)=\mathrm{ev}\bigl(p\mapsto f_p(r_p(\theta))\bigr).
--   $$
--   2. **Prediction limits.** $\Lambda(\theta)$ is the weak limit of $\mathrm{pred}_{b_j}(\theta)$ along $\mathcal U$. It depends norm-continuously on $\theta$, by the uniform coefficient estimate.
--   3. **Detector set.** The union of a finite prefix $z_0,\dots,z_{m-1}$ of the dense sequence with the image $\{\Lambda(\theta)\}$ over the coefficient set. It is nonempty and norm compact.
